a self-lubricating, living bearing that you’re not bending past its design specs. The evidence that this doesn’t cause arthritis comes not just from the Unger self-experiment, but from direct imaging. Real-time MRI and ultrasound show that the pop is a bubble, no grinding occurs, and the cartilage isn’t traumatized. It’s a case where the gut feeling is perfectly wrong, and the science is, in its own way, even cooler: your joints are designed to handle that little party trick just fine.
